  "title": "Service-to-Service Authentication",
  "description": "Secure communication between services with mTLS.",
  "order": 3,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 18,
  "tags": ["mTLS", "service-auth", "zero-trust"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Service-to-service authentication verifies that both parties are who they claim to be. Mutual TLS (mTLS) is the standard approach."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "mTLS",
            "definition": "Mutual TLS: both client and server authenticate with certificates."
          },
          {
            "term": "Service Identity",
            "definition": "The identity of a service (certificate-based)."
          },
          {
            "term": "SPIFFE",
            "definition": "A standard for service identity across platforms."
          },
          {
            "term": "Service Mesh",
            "definition": "Infrastructure that handles service-to-service security (e.g., Istio)."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Authentication Methods"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Method", "Description", "Strength"],
        "rows": [
          ["mTLS", "Certificate-based mutual auth", "Strong"],
          ["JWT", "Token-based auth", "Medium"],
          ["API Key", "Static key", "Weak"],
          ["Network Policy", "IP-based", "Weak"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "mTLS"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "mTLS requires both client and server to present certificates. This ensures both parties are authenticated and the connection is encrypted."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Service Mesh"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A service mesh (Istio, Linkerd) handles mTLS transparently. Sidecar proxies encrypt and authenticate traffic without code changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "SPIFFE"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "SPIFFE (Secure Production Identity Framework for Everyone) provides a standard for service identity. It issues SVIDs (SPIFFE Verifiable Identity Documents) as X.509 certificates or JWTs."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
      "data": {
        "id": "msa-mtls",
        "caption": "Mutual TLS",
        "definition": "sequenceDiagram\n    participant C as Client Service\n    participant S as Server Service\n    C->>S: ClientHello\n    S-->>C: Server Certificate\n    C->>S: Client Certificate\n    S-->>C: Finished\n    Note over C,S: Both authenticated, encrypted channel"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Best Practices"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Design for failure",
          "Keep services loosely coupled",
          "Monitor and observe everything",
          "Automate testing and deployment"
        ]
      }
    },
